From 4099e330cf942159a532aafc1bb1fae82015ccf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:52:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Show what's new once after an update

After an update, the first start shows a dialog centered on the main
window with what changed since the last version seen: the What's new,
Fixes and Upgrade sections of the bundled release notes (now under
data/release-notes), at most the three newest versions, with a pointer
to the full notes for earlier ones. Long text scrolls inside the
dialog, which is at most 70% of the main window's height; it is not
modal. Closing it records the version (update.lastSeenVersion);
quitting with it open shows it again. A fresh install and a rollback
show nothing; an upgrade from a version that did not record the last
one seen shows the current version. When the browser add-on needs an
update, a line on top offers to open the Updates tab.

Tested by unit tests and e2e-whats-new.mjs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
